
Licensing overview for no-OS
============================

Unless a file states otherwise in its own header (which always takes
precedence), source files in this repository are released under the
permissive BSD 3-Clause license found in LICENSE_BSD. This is the
default for the linkable library core and the large majority of the
device drivers.

The files that are NOT under BSD 3-Clause are listed below, grouped by
what they are -- device drivers, example projects, or bundled
third-party libraries -- with the license that applies to each. Anything
not listed here follows the BSD 3-Clause default.


1. Drivers and files not under BSD 3-Clause
-------------------------------------------

A handful of files carry a non-BSD-3-Clause license. In most cases this
is vendor device-API code that cannot be relicensed (1a, 1b); some is
vendor device-API code under the copyleft GPL-2.0 (1d); a few files are
simply under a different permissive license (1c). The driver code is
optional: it is compiled and linked only when you build that driver, so
if you do not build it, none of it ends up in your binary. In the mixed
trees below only the listed vendor-API files differ; the rest of the
driver is BSD 3-Clause. The one non-optional exception is the JESD204
framework (1e), a core subsystem that is GPL-2.0+.

